A||||25||Standard||words to live by||||10||
Z||000000||Standard||04-11-2001||11:56 PM||||Got any little nuggets of wisdom?  Feel free to share them!  Here's a few of mine:<P>If it's stuck, force it.  If it breaks it had to be replaced anyways.<P>If at first you don't succed, get a bigger hammer.<P>And a bunch of stuff from Murphy97   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> great program<P>Schmidt's Law: If you mess with a thing long enough, it'll break.<P>Peer's Law: The solution to the problem changes the problem.<P>Murphy says... Help a man when he is in trouble and he will remember you when he is in trouble again.<P>Schmidt's Observation: All things being equal, a fat person uses more soap than a thin person.<P>Ducharm's Axiom: If you view your problem closely enough you will recognize yourself as part of the problem.<P>Hartley's Second Law: Never go to bed with anybody crazier than you are.<P>Cole's Axiom: The sum of the intelligence on the planet is a constant; the population is growing.<P>Churchill's Commentary on Man: Man will occasionally stumble over the truth, but most of the time he will pick himself up and continue on.<P>Grabel's Law: 2 is not equal to 3 -- not even for large values of 2.<P>Murphy says... Never attribute to malice that which is adequately explained by stupidity.<P>Klipstein's Observation: Any product cut to length will be too short.<P>Gerrold's Law: A little ignorance can go a long way.<P>Third Law of Survival: To protect your position, fire the fastest rising employees first.<P>Cole's Law: Thinly sliced cabbage.<BR>Corry's Law: Paper is always strongest at the perforations.<P>Flap's Law: Any inanimate object, regardless of its composition or configuration, may be expected to perform at any time in a totally unexpected manner for reasons that are either entirely obscure or completely mysterious.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I have alot more of these, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 04-11-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||btoth||04-12-2001||12:05 AM||||Please post 'em! Their halarious!  BTW, where'd you find these?||||reg||10
